{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Algebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Algebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.cocycle_of_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.cocycle_of_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Algebra.lean#L133-L169","doc":"**The mixed-derivative identity is the cocycle identity (generic field).** Differentiating\nthe five-term relation once in `y` and once in `x̄` gives a three-term identity in the values\n`p, r, s` of the second-derivative coefficient `β` at `a = y/x`, `ab`, `b = (1-x)/(1-y)`. Here `X, Y`\nstand for the conjugates of `x, y`. That identity is the nonzero multiple\n`x(Y-1) / (y(X-1)(X-Y)(x-y))` of the cocycle identity for `ρ = β·N`, `N(z) = z Z (1-z)(1-Z)`.\nPure field algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.two_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.two_term","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Algebra.lean#L71-L131","doc":"**The two-term relation is algebraic.** Over any field, with values in any additive group:\ninversion oddness and the five-term relation give `3 • (φ t + φ (1 - t)) = 0` for `t ≠ 0, 1, 2`\nwith `t² - t + 1 ≠ 0`. The proof sums the four five-term instances\n`(t, (1-t)⁻¹)`, `(t, t/(t-1))`, `(t, (t-1)/t)`, `(1-t, (1-t)⁻¹)`. These instances were found by a\nlinear-algebra search over five-term instances with Möbius-related arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.five_term_rearranged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.five_term_rearranged","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Algebra.lean#L49-L69","doc":"**The rearranged five-term relation.** Over any field, with values in any additive\ngroup: if `φ` is inversion-odd on `F ∖ {0,1}` and satisfies Suslin's five-term relation,\nthen\n`φ x = φ y - φ (y/x) - φ ((1 - y⁻¹)/(1 - x⁻¹)) + φ ((1 - y)/(1 - x))`.\nThe variable `x` now occurs only in denominators. This is the identity the regularity\nargument integrates against a bump function in `y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.flip_args","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.flip_args","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Algebra.lean#L34-L45","doc":"The two \"flipped\" five-term arguments `(1 - y⁻¹)/(1 - x⁻¹)` and `(1 - y)/(1 - x)` avoid\n`0` and `1` whenever `x, y ≠ 1` and `x ≠ y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.one_sub_inv_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.one_sub_inv_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Algebra.lean#L31-L32","signatureChunk":0}]}